{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונשמע", :translit "ve-nishma", :gloss "and it shall be heard"} {:he "כל אשר דבר ה' נעשה ונשמע", :translit "kol asher diber Hashem na'aseh ve-nishma", :gloss "all that Hashem has spoken we will do and we will hear"} {:he "ונשמע פתגם המלך", :translit "u-nishma pegam ha-melekh", :gloss "and the king's decree shall be heard"} {:he "ונשמע קולו", :translit "ve-nishma kolo", :gloss "and his voice shall be heard"} {:he "כי רבה היא", :translit "ki rabbah hi", :gloss "for she is great"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ונשמע" "כל אשר דבר ה' נעשה ונשמע" "ונשמע פתגם המלך"]}], :frame {:text "Rabba teaches that reading the Megillah takes precedence over both Tefillah and Avodah (Megillah 3b). Israel's declaration 'we will do and we will hear' at Sinai (Exodus 24:7) corresponds to Tefillah and Avodah, since the verse 'and his voice shall be heard' describes the High Priest's service. The Megillah reading corresponds to 'the king's decree shall be heard' (Esther 1:20). The Targum renders 'ki rabbah hi' (Esther 1:20) as 'for it is precious/important,' signaling the Megillah's greater precedence.", :sources ["Megillah 3b" "Exodus 24:7" "Esther 1:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ובצאתו", :translit "u-vetzo'o", :gloss "and in his going out"} {:he "והיו את המלך בבואו ובצאתו", :translit "ve-hayu et ha-melekh be-vo'o u-vetzo'o", :gloss "and they were with the king in his coming and in his going out"} {:he "ובצאתו ולא ימית", :translit "u-vetzo'o ve-lo yamit", :gloss "and in his going out and he shall not die"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ובצאתו" "והיו את המלך בבואו ובצאתו"]} {:kind :other, :note "The second occurrence (2 Chronicles 24:5) guards Joash so he is not killed; this parallels the High Priest's safe exit."}], :frame {:text "When Joash was hidden as a child in the Temple, guards surrounded him when he came and went, lest Athaliah kill him (2 Chronicles 22:11–12). The phrase 'they were with the king in his coming and in his going out' appears in 2 Chronicles 24:5. Ba'al HaTurim links this to the High Priest's safe exit from the Holy of Holies on Yom Kippur, when he must emerge without dying, as the service demands (Leviticus 16:17, Yoma 53a).", :sources ["2 Chronicles 22:11–12" "2 Chronicles 24:5" "Leviticus 16:17" "Yoma 53a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ונשמע" "כל אשר דבר ה' נעשה ונשמע" "ונשמע פתגם המלך"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ונשמע", :refs ["Exodus 24:7" "Exodus 28:35" "Joshua 2:11" "Jeremiah 35:8" "Jeremiah 35:10" "Esther 1:20"], :n 6, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כל אשר דבר ה' נעשה ונשמע", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ונשמע פתגם המלך", :refs ["Esther 1:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ובצאתו" "והיו את המלך בבואו ובצאתו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ובצאתו", :refs ["Exodus 28:35" "2 Chronicles 23:7"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והיו את המלך בבואו ובצאתו", :refs ["2 Chronicles 23:7"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "The second occurrence (2 Chronicles 24:5) guards Joash so he is not killed; this parallels the High Priest's safe exit.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:06.350351153Z", :model "glm-5.2"}